WEBVTT

1
00:44:50.146 --> 00:44:51.146
Sit down comfortably.

2
00:44:51.146 --> 00:45:05.986
God is for you, God loves you, God has the best in store for you.

3
00:45:05.986 --> 00:45:08.906
That is what we will be talking about all summer long.

4
00:45:08.906 --> 00:45:12.546
God provides, God wants to take care of you.

5
00:45:12.546 --> 00:45:19.986
And this week I came across a beautiful chapter in Ezekiel, chapter 34.

6
00:45:19.986 --> 00:45:27.386
That whole chapter is about the Good Shepherd, that God wants to be a Shepherd for us and

7
00:45:27.386 --> 00:45:30.826
lead us to green pastures.

8
00:45:30.826 --> 00:45:38.266
The fact that Jesus is our Shepherd and that whole chapter beautifully shows what God's heart

9
00:45:38.266 --> 00:45:39.266
is like.

10
00:45:39.266 --> 00:45:47.546
And Ezekiel receives this as a revelation from God while he is in Babylon.

11
00:45:47.546 --> 00:45:50.706
Actually the low point for the whole people of Israel.

12
00:45:50.706 --> 00:45:58.466
God had chosen the people of Israel, made from Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, led them from Egypt to

13
00:45:58.466 --> 00:46:00.066
the promised land.

14
00:46:00.066 --> 00:46:07.026
And then many generations later it has gone so wrong that God has no choice but to remove the

15
00:46:07.026 --> 00:46:15.026
whole nation and take them into exile to Babylon, and there they are

16
00:46:15.026 --> 00:46:16.306
at the low point.

17
00:46:16.306 --> 00:46:24.226
And then Ezekiel receives this revelation and the whole chapter is fantastic but we cannot

18
00:46:24.226 --> 00:46:29.346
read it now, but I want to read together with you from verse 26.

19
00:46:29.346 --> 00:46:37.986
Everything on my hill, says God, will be for them, they are the people of Israel, his sheep.

20
00:46:37.986 --> 00:46:40.226
It will go well with them.

21
00:46:40.226 --> 00:46:46.866
I will give rain in due time, delightful gentle rain showers in the rainy season.

22
00:46:46.866 --> 00:46:53.986
The trees and the fields will yield abundant harvests, the sheep will live safely in the land.

23
00:46:53.986 --> 00:46:54.986
They will be able to live.

24
00:46:55.386 --> 00:46:59.306
I will rescue them from the power of those who mistreat them.

25
00:46:59.306 --> 00:47:02.586
Then they will realize that I am the Lord.

26
00:47:02.586 --> 00:47:07.946
They will no longer be prey to the other nations, the wild animals will no longer eat them but they will dwell safely without anyone frightening them.

27
00:47:07.946 --> 00:47:12.906
There will be such great harvests that everyone will talk about them.

28
00:47:12.906 --> 00:47:19.626
No one will die of hunger anymore, no nation will mock them anymore.

29
00:47:19.626 --> 00:47:24.506
They will realize that I am their Lord God with them and that they are my people, says the Lord.

30
00:47:25.386 --> 00:47:32.506
You are my sheep, the people for whom I care.

31
00:47:32.506 --> 00:47:38.506
You are my people and I am your God, says the Lord.

32
00:47:38.506 --> 00:47:43.386
This he said about the people of Israel, but he also said this about you.

33
00:47:43.386 --> 00:47:48.506
This whole chapter is a provision, a prophecy, a foreshadowing of Jesus.

34
00:47:49.066 --> 00:47:57.306
That ultimately Jesus comes and gathers his sheep together just as we are gathered here now.

35
00:47:57.306 --> 00:48:05.306
And as we come together this Sunday all over the world as his flock, as his sheep.

36
00:48:05.306 --> 00:48:12.346
Under his leadership, under his shepherding.

37
00:48:12.346 --> 00:48:15.546
He loves us, he has the best for us, for us collectively and for each of us personally.

38
00:48:15.546 --> 00:48:22.746
But sometimes we have a very wrong idea of what it looks like that God cares for us.

39
00:48:25.786 --> 00:48:31.066
Sometimes we are far too focused on our own interests and I want it to be better and I want that.

40
00:48:31.066 --> 00:48:37.786


41
00:48:37.786 --> 00:48:42.186
And God wants to take care of this for you, and I want to have that too, and so on.

42
00:48:42.266 --> 00:48:48.186
But just imagine that you have a teenager as a parent who has completely gone astray.

43
00:48:48.186 --> 00:48:53.546
He is into drugs, going to prostitutes, partying hard.

44
00:48:53.546 --> 00:48:57.386
He is making a complete mess of his life.

45
00:48:59.146 --> 00:49:01.786
What do you do as a parent?

46
00:49:01.786 --> 00:49:05.626
Are you going to give him everything he asks for?

47
00:49:05.626 --> 00:49:07.946
More money?

48
00:49:07.946 --> 00:49:10.506
So he can buy more drugs?

49
00:49:10.586 --> 00:49:17.946
Or are you as a parent focused on guiding him, no matter how difficult it may be,

50
00:49:17.946 --> 00:49:22.826
trying to help him get back on the right path?

51
00:49:22.826 --> 00:49:29.226
So you are not going to give him everything he needs, because you know that will ruin his life.

52
00:49:29.226 --> 00:49:31.066
And it is the same with God.

53
00:49:31.066 --> 00:49:38.506
His care for us is not just giving us what we want, but giving us what we need.

54
00:49:38.506 --> 00:49:40.266
He gives what is good for us.

55
00:49:40.266 --> 00:49:45.066
He gives what makes our lives beautiful and complete.

56
00:49:45.066 --> 00:49:53.226
And it is very important that we live in His way and manage our finances in His way as well.

57
00:49:53.226 --> 00:49:55.546
And that includes generosity.

58
00:49:55.546 --> 00:49:57.626
Caring for the people around you.

59
00:49:57.626 --> 00:50:04.826
If God wants the whole people, the whole flock, to do well, then He wants to use us for that and engage us in it.

60
00:50:04.826 --> 00:50:07.706
He also wants us to be good to each other.

61
00:50:07.786 --> 00:50:11.386
Also financially for those who are struggling.

62
00:50:11.386 --> 00:50:22.586
And when you learn to be generous, then God sees, look, this is my son, my daughter who is joining in my plan of prosperity and provision.

63
00:50:22.586 --> 00:50:26.186
And then He will give you abundance and take care of you.

64
00:50:26.186 --> 00:50:33.066
Really, because He knows that you are then working with Him to ensure that things go well in this world.

65
00:50:33.066 --> 00:50:36.266
So live His way, be generous.

66
00:50:37.706 --> 00:50:39.866
Thank you.

67
00:51:07.706 --> 00:51:12.986
Good afternoon August, those are the total periods of the children's camp and the youth camp combined.

68
00:51:12.986 --> 00:51:18.586
The children's camp ends somewhere on Wednesday and then I think the youth camp starts on Wednesday.

69
00:51:18.586 --> 00:51:22.426
But the call is to sign up your children.

70
00:51:22.426 --> 00:51:27.946
It comes in bits and pieces, it will just continue, the children's camps and the youth camps.

71
00:51:27.946 --> 00:51:35.866
I can tell you, I used to go on children's camp and youth camp often and it was always very special, I think.

72
00:51:37.866 --> 00:51:43.466
It was always a lot of fun and yes, you actually form friendships there for life.

73
00:51:43.466 --> 00:51:46.986
And since we know God, you form friendships for eternity.

74
00:51:48.586 --> 00:51:51.946
Another call is also real man camp.

75
00:51:53.546 --> 00:51:55.546
Voila, look at that.

76
00:51:56.426 --> 00:52:00.906
September 16th that will take place and it is also the intention to sign up.

77
00:52:00.986 --> 00:52:10.986
Last year we were quite a considerable group and it is called real man, but we are not talking about real men as it goes in the world.

78
00:52:10.986 --> 00:52:20.506
We are talking about men of God who will come together, share something special, draw closer to God, who can become the heads of their families.

79
00:52:20.506 --> 00:52:24.906
But I am getting ahead of the facts, so also sign up.

80
00:52:24.986 --> 00:52:31.946
And preferably also, that can all be done via the church's website, openkerk.com, it is also in the app, the links.

81
00:52:31.946 --> 00:52:39.146
And while you give up, it is the intention that you also make the payment by August 1st.

82
00:52:39.146 --> 00:52:42.826
So those were the announcements.

83
00:52:42.826 --> 00:52:48.986
And then I would actually like to invite Chris to honor us with a beautiful sermon.

84
00:52:54.986 --> 00:52:56.986
Thank you.

85
00:53:14.986 --> 00:53:16.986
Delightful.

86
00:53:16.986 --> 00:53:18.986
God is so good.

87
00:53:19.066 --> 00:53:21.066
And He remains good.

88
00:53:21.066 --> 00:53:23.066
And His goodness lasts forever.

89
00:53:23.066 --> 00:53:25.066
Hallelujah.

90
00:53:27.066 --> 00:53:37.066
On God's mountain, where God provides, it is so beautiful to see that God provides, He cares for us, He loves us.

91
00:53:37.146 --> 00:53:47.146
And actually the event we started with, also about that mountain, what we have told is, by the way Ben, thanks.

92
00:53:47.146 --> 00:53:51.146
It's strange to have to say that when you are playing along yourself.

93
00:53:51.146 --> 00:53:53.146
Thanks.

94
00:53:53.146 --> 00:53:55.146
Please have a seat.

95
00:53:55.146 --> 00:53:57.146
Super.

96
00:53:57.146 --> 00:53:59.146
It is wonderful to be able to glorify God.

97
00:53:59.146 --> 00:54:01.146
He deserves it, truly.

98
00:54:01.226 --> 00:54:09.226
Abraham and Isaac were on that mountain and they also showed the image of the great gift of the Father.

99
00:54:09.226 --> 00:54:15.226
They showed that the gift of the Father was Jesus, is Jesus, and remains Jesus.

100
00:54:15.226 --> 00:54:17.226
Jesus as a sacrifice.

101
00:54:17.226 --> 00:54:23.226
And actually, I want to unpack that great gift together with you today.

102
00:54:23.226 --> 00:54:29.226
It is beautiful to unpack Jesus as a gift layer by layer.

103
00:54:29.306 --> 00:54:31.306
And the beautiful thing about it is, it is lasting.

104
00:54:31.306 --> 00:54:33.306
That too is lasting.

105
00:54:33.306 --> 00:54:35.306
We can keep unpacking Jesus.

106
00:54:35.306 --> 00:54:39.306
He comes, He is eternal, and He continually reveals something new about Himself.

107
00:54:39.306 --> 00:54:45.306
And it is always a revelation of Him that you need day by day.

108
00:54:45.306 --> 00:54:49.306
And that is something beautiful that God gives.

109
00:54:49.306 --> 00:54:52.306
And He gives that in His love.

110
00:54:52.306 --> 00:54:56.306
And His love is not unconditional but it is inexhaustible.

111
00:54:56.386 --> 00:55:01.386
For all the conditions attached to that love, Jesus has fulfilled.

112
00:55:01.386 --> 00:55:05.386
Jesus is the condition for God's love.

113
00:55:05.386 --> 00:55:08.386
And the only thing we may do is receive it.

114
00:55:08.386 --> 00:55:13.386
And that we may receive it in complete surrender to Him.

115
00:55:13.386 --> 00:55:16.386
And that is what we want to zoom in on today.

116
00:55:16.386 --> 00:55:19.386
And we may do that in complete trust and dependence.

117
00:55:19.386 --> 00:55:24.386
For actually, surrender is a mix of trust and dependence.

118
00:55:24.466 --> 00:55:27.466
And that is something God wants to give us.

119
00:55:27.466 --> 00:55:31.466
And it is something lasting. It is something more than a happening.

120
00:55:31.466 --> 00:55:34.466
Or something we do.

121
00:55:34.466 --> 00:55:40.466
And I also pray that today this unpacking of Jesus may bring us closer to Him.

122
00:55:40.466 --> 00:55:43.466
And that it may also give us something for these summer months.

123
00:55:43.466 --> 00:55:46.466
Where we might perhaps have more time.

124
00:55:46.466 --> 00:55:50.466
And maybe we can also make a bit more time for Jesus. A few times.

125
00:55:50.466 --> 00:55:53.466
For it is needed. It is needed. We need Jesus.

126
00:55:54.466 --> 00:55:57.466
And I enjoy unpacking Jesus.

127
00:55:57.466 --> 00:56:00.466
And I have taken a piece of text from the Bible for that.

128
00:56:00.466 --> 00:56:02.466
And that is John 15.

129
00:56:02.466 --> 00:56:05.466
And I am fond of John 15.

130
00:56:05.466 --> 00:56:08.466
Really completely fond of John 15.

131
00:56:08.466 --> 00:56:10.466
And I want to read it out loud.

132
00:56:10.466 --> 00:56:13.466
Jesus says there, I am the true vine.

133
00:56:13.466 --> 00:56:16.466
And my Father is the vinedresser.

134
00:56:16.466 --> 00:56:18.466
He is the farmer.

135
00:56:18.466 --> 00:56:23.466
Every branch that does not bear fruit, He takes away. He prunes it.

136
00:56:23.466 --> 00:56:28.466
And every branch that bears fruit, He prunes it.

137
00:56:28.466 --> 00:56:31.466
So the one that does not bear fruit, He takes away.

138
00:56:31.466 --> 00:56:34.466
And every branch that bears fruit, He prunes it back.

139
00:56:34.466 --> 00:56:37.466
So that it may bear more fruit again.

140
00:56:37.466 --> 00:56:42.466
And then He says, amazing, you are already clean because of everything I have said to you.

141
00:56:42.466 --> 00:56:45.466
He says, remain in me, then I will remain in you.

142
00:56:46.466 --> 00:56:51.466
A branch that does not remain on the vine cannot bear fruit by itself.

143
00:56:51.466 --> 00:56:55.466
And so you cannot bear fruit unless you remain in me.

144
00:56:55.466 --> 00:56:59.466
And once again, I am the vine and you are the branches.

145
00:56:59.466 --> 00:57:04.466
If anyone remains in me and I in him, he will bear much fruit.

146
00:57:04.466 --> 00:57:06.466
But without me you can do nothing.

147
00:57:06.466 --> 00:57:09.466
Very important, without Jesus we can do nothing.

148
00:57:09.466 --> 00:57:14.466
Whoever does not remain in me is thrown away like a branch and withers.

149
00:57:14.466 --> 00:57:18.466
He is gathered with the other branches and thrown into the fire and burned.

150
00:57:18.466 --> 00:57:22.466
If you remain in me, my words will remain in you.

151
00:57:22.466 --> 00:57:26.466
And then you can ask for whatever you want and it will happen.

152
00:57:26.466 --> 00:57:29.466
The greatness of my Father will become visible.

153
00:57:29.466 --> 00:57:32.466
When you bear much fruit and are my disciples.

154
00:57:32.466 --> 00:57:35.466
I have loved you as the Father has loved me.

155
00:57:35.466 --> 00:57:38.466
Remain in my love.

156
00:57:38.466 --> 00:57:41.466
You remain in my love if you keep my commandments.

157
00:57:41.466 --> 00:57:46.466
Just as I have kept my Father's commandments and remain in his love.

158
00:57:46.466 --> 00:57:51.466
And this I say to you to give you my joy and then your joy will be complete.

159
00:57:51.466 --> 00:57:56.466
My command is that you love one another as I have loved you.

160
00:57:56.466 --> 00:58:01.466
There is no greater love than to give your life for your friends.

161
00:58:01.466 --> 00:58:04.466
You are my friends when you do what I say.

162
00:58:04.466 --> 00:58:07.466
I love Jesus, wonderful this text.

163
00:58:07.466 --> 00:58:10.466
I no longer call you slaves, that has just been said again.

164
00:58:10.466 --> 00:58:13.466
For a slave does not know what his master is doing.

165
00:58:13.466 --> 00:58:19.466
I call you friends, because I have made known to you everything that I heard from the Father.

166
00:58:19.466 --> 00:58:23.466
You did not choose me, but I chose you.

167
00:58:23.466 --> 00:58:26.466
So Jesus says to us today.

168
00:58:26.466 --> 00:58:30.466
I have commanded you to go and bear fruit.

169
00:58:30.466 --> 00:58:32.466
Fruit that will last.

170
00:58:32.466 --> 00:58:37.466
Whatever you ask the Father in my name, he will give you.

171
00:58:37.466 --> 00:58:40.466
And once again, this I command you.

172
00:58:40.466 --> 00:58:42.466
Love one another.

173
00:58:43.466 --> 00:58:48.466
I have a few more pictures today.

174
00:58:48.466 --> 00:58:52.466
And I would like to show the first picture.

175
00:58:52.466 --> 00:58:56.466
And as you can see, this is the vine.

176
00:58:56.466 --> 00:58:59.466
If you know a grape plant, I love these plants.

177
00:58:59.466 --> 00:59:03.466
These plants are amazing, they are a gift from heaven.

178
00:59:03.466 --> 00:59:07.466
And if you look at that vine, that is Jesus.

179
00:59:07.466 --> 00:59:13.466
If you look at those very thin branches, to which those large clusters hang, that is us.

180
00:59:13.466 --> 00:59:15.466
Thin branches.

181
00:59:15.466 --> 00:59:17.466
It is very important to remember that.

182
00:59:17.466 --> 00:59:21.466
And the Father is the vine grower, that is the farmer.

183
00:59:21.466 --> 00:59:24.466
He takes care of this.

184
00:59:24.466 --> 00:59:31.466
And the most beautiful thing about this is that Jesus is at our service.

185
00:59:32.466 --> 00:59:36.466
That is so beautiful, Jesus is at our service.

186
00:59:36.466 --> 00:59:39.466
He remains at our service.

187
00:59:39.466 --> 00:59:43.466
This is really important to realize.

188
00:59:43.466 --> 00:59:48.466
And he is also at service for the fruits that we may bear.

189
00:59:48.466 --> 00:59:54.466
And ultimately also for those for whom those fruits are, for the farmer, for the vine grower.

190
00:59:54.466 --> 00:59:58.466
So he actually enters into a partnership with us.

191
00:59:59.466 --> 01:00:07.466
And we, we are asked to also be at service for that fruit and also for that farmer.

192
01:00:07.466 --> 01:00:12.466
That is actually the partnership, so to speak, that we may have with God.

193
01:00:12.466 --> 01:00:17.466
And I would actually like another picture, the next picture please, Elmar.

194
01:00:17.466 --> 01:00:18.466
Thanks.

195
01:00:18.466 --> 01:00:20.466
What do I have here again?

196
01:00:20.466 --> 01:00:21.466
What do you think, what kind of picture is that?

197
01:00:21.466 --> 01:00:22.466
Doesn't even look like a vine.

198
01:00:22.466 --> 01:00:28.466
No, but we once went to look in the area of, yes, very beautiful pictures.

199
01:00:28.466 --> 01:00:31.466
And they have here marlstone.

200
01:00:31.466 --> 01:00:38.466
And those stones and marl and all the nutrients are in that water.

201
01:00:38.466 --> 01:00:40.466
And what does Jesus do?

202
01:00:40.466 --> 01:00:45.466
He draws from that crazy ground, where there is water and sometimes it's so difficult.

203
01:00:45.466 --> 01:00:48.466
A vine can sometimes go so deep to fetch water.

204
01:00:49.466 --> 01:00:54.466
They have measured roots that are almost a kilometer long.

205
01:00:54.466 --> 01:00:56.466
That is really, really madness.

206
01:00:56.466 --> 01:00:57.466
That is truly a plant.

207
01:00:57.466 --> 01:01:00.466
Once it starts to grow and it is thirsty, it will go.

208
01:01:00.466 --> 01:01:02.466
And that is Jesus.

209
01:01:02.466 --> 01:01:04.466
Jesus is that vine.

210
01:01:04.466 --> 01:01:05.466
He is thirsty.

211
01:01:05.466 --> 01:01:07.466
He wants to nourish you and me.

212
01:01:07.466 --> 01:01:10.466
And as you can see, there is also a little shell in there and so on.

213
01:01:10.466 --> 01:01:13.466
And all those nutrients, he takes with him.

214
01:01:13.466 --> 01:01:16.466
And he provides the living water.

215
01:01:16.466 --> 01:01:19.466
And we need the living water, day by day.

216
01:01:21.466 --> 01:01:28.466
And I actually want to elaborate a bit more on Jesus as the vine.

217
01:01:28.466 --> 01:01:38.466
Because he doesn't just want to be our God for a moment, our friend, as he just said.

218
01:01:38.466 --> 01:01:40.466
But he wants to be that and remain that.

219
01:01:40.466 --> 01:01:42.466
He wants to be that continuously.

220
01:01:43.466 --> 01:01:48.466
It is also true, if you are not connected to that vine, then it simply goes wrong.

221
01:01:48.466 --> 01:01:49.466
Very simple, with us.

222
01:01:49.466 --> 01:01:54.466
And Jesus, who came to earth, went to his friends and said, come and follow me.

223
01:01:54.466 --> 01:01:55.466
And they came.

224
01:01:55.466 --> 01:01:56.466
And that was good.

225
01:01:56.466 --> 01:01:57.466
That was fine.

226
01:01:57.466 --> 01:02:04.466
But now, just before Jesus went to the cross, he says to his friends, come and remain in me.

227
01:02:04.466 --> 01:02:07.466
So first you have, come and follow me.

228
01:02:07.466 --> 01:02:11.466
And then you have what Jesus asks, come and remain in me.

229
01:02:12.466 --> 01:02:16.466
And this is what we as a church need to remain in him.

230
01:02:16.466 --> 01:02:18.466
And to dwell in him.

231
01:02:18.466 --> 01:02:25.466
And to seek Jesus completely and to get to work with that.

232
01:02:25.466 --> 01:02:33.466
For it is not that he would have bought and paid for us just for a little while.

233
01:02:33.466 --> 01:02:35.466
He has bought and paid for us with a purpose.

234
01:02:35.466 --> 01:02:39.466
Of course, our salvation and our redemption are very important.

235
01:02:39.466 --> 01:02:42.466
For otherwise we would still be stuck in the mess.

236
01:02:42.466 --> 01:02:48.466
But what Jesus wants is that he wants to give us himself.

237
01:02:48.466 --> 01:02:50.466
He wants to keep giving us himself.

238
01:02:50.466 --> 01:02:53.466
And this is so important, that we realize this well.

239
01:02:53.466 --> 01:02:56.466
He has bought and paid for us.

240
01:02:56.466 --> 01:03:06.466
And he has given himself, but now he is at the right hand of the Father and he wants to keep giving himself to us.

241
01:03:07.466 --> 01:03:12.466
And I truly believe that this is a word that Jesus did not tell for nothing.

242
01:03:12.466 --> 01:03:19.466
And what we as a church, as a united church need, individually, that is, alone, ourselves.

243
01:03:19.466 --> 01:03:26.466
If we all do that ourselves, then the church will also thrive well.

244
01:03:26.466 --> 01:03:34.466
But also after that and alongside it, there will be all sorts of other matters that come to the surface, all of which fit into God's plan.

245
01:03:34.466 --> 01:03:39.466
And I want to go further on that later, because otherwise I will reveal it right away, and that is not fun either.

246
01:03:39.466 --> 01:03:44.466
But, come and remain in me.

247
01:03:44.466 --> 01:03:49.466
And I truly believe that we need that revelation of Jesus himself.

248
01:03:49.466 --> 01:03:51.466
That revelation lies therein.

249
01:03:51.466 --> 01:03:55.466
And where does that revelation of Christ begin?

250
01:03:55.466 --> 01:03:57.466
It begins in that vine.

251
01:03:58.466 --> 01:04:07.466
And we are as it were, as a branch, as a small twig, grafted into Jesus.

252
01:04:07.466 --> 01:04:12.466
And what is written in that vine, at the place where we are grafted?

253
01:04:12.466 --> 01:04:14.466
There stands the cross.

254
01:04:14.466 --> 01:04:16.466
Jesus is circumcised of heart.

255
01:04:16.466 --> 01:04:18.466
He is open to us.

256
01:04:18.466 --> 01:04:20.466
He is open to the Father.

257
01:04:20.466 --> 01:04:23.466
Why? Because we must come into that.

258
01:04:23.466 --> 01:04:32.466
But, it is important that we too, in that part of the branch that we are, are also circumcised of heart.

259
01:04:32.466 --> 01:04:38.466
He wants this. He wants us to drink.

260
01:04:38.466 --> 01:04:41.466
Something must start to flow. The living water must be able to enter that branch.

261
01:04:41.466 --> 01:04:45.466
And that is why the cross is so important.

262
01:04:45.466 --> 01:04:50.466
That we do not think of the cross as a one-time event, but that we reflect on this.

263
01:04:50.466 --> 01:04:53.466
And Jesus also gave the communion for that purpose.

264
01:04:53.466 --> 01:04:56.466
He also gave his Word, he gave his Spirit.

265
01:04:56.466 --> 01:04:59.466
It is so important to grasp this.

266
01:04:59.466 --> 01:05:05.466
And if we remain in him, we will be filled with Jesus.

267
01:05:05.466 --> 01:05:07.466
So full that it must come out.

268
01:05:07.466 --> 01:05:10.466
And, yes, that is important.

269
01:05:10.466 --> 01:05:15.466
This is what Jesus wants. He wants to come out of us.

270
01:05:15.466 --> 01:05:18.466
That we present Jesus. That we may show Jesus.

271
01:05:19.466 --> 01:05:25.466
And we need it as well. We need it as nourishment, as a breeding ground.

272
01:05:25.466 --> 01:05:30.466
Otherwise, we will die. You can see that with those branches that simply wither away.

273
01:05:30.466 --> 01:05:33.466
If we are not in Jesus, then there is no life in us.

274
01:05:33.466 --> 01:05:35.466
Without him, we can do nothing.

275
01:05:35.466 --> 01:05:38.466
And if we then do something, it is completely pointless.

276
01:05:38.466 --> 01:05:43.466
And, yes, the point is that we do not draw from that.

277
01:05:43.466 --> 01:05:48.466
Even if Jesus meets all those conditions we just talked about.

278
01:05:48.466 --> 01:05:52.466
We still need Jesus to be able to do this.

279
01:05:52.466 --> 01:05:54.466
We do not draw that from ourselves.

280
01:05:54.466 --> 01:05:56.466
Because we are human.

281
01:05:56.466 --> 01:05:57.466
And Paul says very clearly as well.

282
01:05:57.466 --> 01:06:03.466
As humans, we cannot manage with a limited, sinful nature to remain in Him.

283
01:06:03.466 --> 01:06:06.466
Through our own efforts, our own drive, our own way.

284
01:06:06.466 --> 01:06:11.466
Our own wisdom, our own stubbornness, our shortcomings, corruption.

285
01:06:11.466 --> 01:06:13.466
We will fail time and again.

286
01:06:13.466 --> 01:06:15.466
No one is perfect, not even one.

287
01:06:15.466 --> 01:06:18.466
And we have all sinned and become useless.

288
01:06:18.466 --> 01:06:20.466
All branches that have dried up.

289
01:06:20.466 --> 01:06:23.466
All ready for lighting the barbecue.

290
01:06:24.466 --> 01:06:27.466
And then you say, well, Chris, thank you for the Word.

291
01:06:27.466 --> 01:06:29.466
We're going to the fries.

292
01:06:30.466 --> 01:06:32.466
But the point is, it is true.

293
01:06:32.466 --> 01:06:35.466
There is no goodness in us.

294
01:06:36.466 --> 01:06:38.466
We are corrupt.

295
01:06:38.466 --> 01:06:40.466
Only, we need Jesus.

296
01:06:40.466 --> 01:06:45.466
And the beautiful thing about it is, and that is the most beautiful thing God gives.

297
01:06:45.466 --> 01:06:47.466
With God, all things are possible.

298
01:06:47.466 --> 01:06:52.466
For He can also make a dead branch alive again.

299
01:06:53.466 --> 01:06:57.466
And this is, it sounds so simple with Jesus.

300
01:06:57.466 --> 01:06:59.466
These words sound very simple.

301
01:06:59.466 --> 01:07:02.466
But it is so well thought out.

302
01:07:02.466 --> 01:07:05.466
And it is so important and it is so true.

303
01:07:05.466 --> 01:07:09.466
We can want and try everything, but without him we can do nothing.

304
01:07:09.466 --> 01:07:12.466
Jesus went to the cross.

305
01:07:12.466 --> 01:07:17.466
And he is the foundation of our salvation and redemption.

306
01:07:17.466 --> 01:07:19.466
In God's interest.

307
01:07:19.466 --> 01:07:24.466
But if we remain in him, then salvation and redemption are just the beginning.

308
01:07:24.466 --> 01:07:28.466
You can actually almost compare it to what Robert just mentioned.

309
01:07:28.466 --> 01:07:32.466
I have a slightly different parable.

310
01:07:32.466 --> 01:07:34.466
So if you were to have a multinational corporation.

311
01:07:34.466 --> 01:07:37.466
It simply has, I don't know how many companies, a whole bunch of children.

312
01:07:37.466 --> 01:07:43.466
And when he looks at his children, he could leave them his inheritance.

313
01:07:43.466 --> 01:07:45.466
He could work and do.

314
01:07:45.466 --> 01:07:47.466
And make it even bigger, make it even bigger.

315
01:07:47.466 --> 01:07:49.466
But when the point of inheritance comes.

316
01:07:49.466 --> 01:07:51.466
And he gives that inheritance to those children.

317
01:07:51.466 --> 01:07:54.466
Then those children really don't know how to deal with it.

318
01:07:54.466 --> 01:07:57.466
So what is very important is.

319
01:07:57.466 --> 01:08:00.466
Is that what God wants to teach us.

320
01:08:00.466 --> 01:08:04.466
Is how we should handle the inheritance that God wants to give us.

321
01:08:04.466 --> 01:08:07.466
And that is really huge, what God wants to give us.

322
01:08:07.466 --> 01:08:09.466
How we may deal with that.

323
01:08:09.466 --> 01:08:11.466
And it is in this way.

324
01:08:11.466 --> 01:08:14.466
He wants to prepare us, for he wants us to be ready.

325
01:08:14.466 --> 01:08:17.466
He wants us to be ready in every situation.

326
01:08:17.466 --> 01:08:20.466
Whether things are going well, or whether they are going poorly.

327
01:08:20.466 --> 01:08:25.466
Whether you have little.

328
01:08:25.466 --> 01:08:30.466
And even if you have much, and also have much to do for him.

329
01:08:30.466 --> 01:08:33.466
He wants to prepare us as a king.

330
01:08:33.466 --> 01:08:39.466
And he wants to prepare us to shape his kingdom.

331
01:08:39.466 --> 01:08:42.466
He wants us to be partners in his kingdom.

332
01:08:42.466 --> 01:08:45.466
That means you need to have a different mindset.

333
01:08:45.466 --> 01:08:50.466
Than the mindset that is presented to us in many other ways.

334
01:08:50.466 --> 01:08:55.466
And we can only receive that mindset from Jesus.

335
01:08:55.466 --> 01:08:58.466
And the cross is that place.

336
01:08:58.466 --> 01:09:00.466
The cross is that place.

337
01:09:01.466 --> 01:09:04.466
And I am so glad for Jesus.

338
01:09:04.466 --> 01:09:06.466
And also glad for Paul.

339
01:09:06.466 --> 01:09:09.466
For Paul writes very clearly about that, even in one sentence.

340
01:09:09.466 --> 01:09:13.466
He says, no longer I, but Christ lives in me.

341
01:09:13.466 --> 01:09:15.466
And this is what is needed.

342
01:09:15.466 --> 01:09:18.466
That Jesus lives in us.

343
01:09:18.466 --> 01:09:22.466
If we let ourselves be grafted into the true vine in full surrender.

344
01:09:22.466 --> 01:09:26.466
Then we have complete access to everything in Jesus.

345
01:09:27.466 --> 01:09:31.466
Would he not give us everything with Jesus, says Paul?

346
01:09:31.466 --> 01:09:33.466
That is bombastically much.

347
01:09:33.466 --> 01:09:37.466
We can't do that in one day, so to speak, just like that.

348
01:09:37.466 --> 01:09:39.466
Or in one moment.

349
01:09:39.466 --> 01:09:41.466
Then we would explode.

350
01:09:41.466 --> 01:09:42.466
But it is enough.

351
01:09:42.466 --> 01:09:46.466
It is so bombastically much that for every moment in eternity,

352
01:09:46.466 --> 01:09:48.466
more than enough.

353
01:09:51.466 --> 01:09:54.466
And that is something wonderful.

354
01:09:56.466 --> 01:09:58.466
But how does that work exactly?

355
01:09:58.466 --> 01:10:01.466
How can I be full of Jesus every moment of the day?

356
01:10:01.466 --> 01:10:02.466
I am busy, busy, busy.

357
01:10:02.466 --> 01:10:05.466
Families, friends, work, church.

358
01:10:05.466 --> 01:10:06.466
Good question.

359
01:10:06.466 --> 01:10:08.466
Thank you.

360
01:10:08.466 --> 01:10:11.466
It is such that God has given us time.

361
01:10:11.466 --> 01:10:14.466
He has also given us the factor of time.

362
01:10:14.466 --> 01:10:15.466
He has made a day for us.

363
01:10:15.466 --> 01:10:17.466
And he has made a night for us.

364
01:10:17.466 --> 01:10:20.466
If we do not sleep, things go wrong.

365
01:10:20.466 --> 01:10:22.466
That is simply our nature.

366
01:10:22.466 --> 01:10:24.466
Just as God intended us to be.

367
01:10:25.466 --> 01:10:27.466
But he has placed a mystery in that.

368
01:10:27.466 --> 01:10:30.466
You receive a new day from God every time.

369
01:10:30.466 --> 01:10:36.466
And it is very beautiful to see that we may eat every day.

370
01:10:36.466 --> 01:10:39.466
We may drink every day.

371
01:10:39.466 --> 01:10:41.466
And that is here too.

372
01:10:41.466 --> 01:10:44.466
So that is not only physical, but it is also spiritual.

373
01:10:44.466 --> 01:10:47.466
And this is what he also gives us as a gift.

374
01:10:47.466 --> 01:10:50.466
He gives us Jesus as food and drink.

375
01:10:50.466 --> 01:10:52.466
As bread and wine.

376
01:10:52.466 --> 01:10:53.466
As living water.

377
01:10:53.466 --> 01:10:58.466
And all those other examples that are given about Jesus.

378
01:10:58.466 --> 01:11:02.466
But you simply need to seize those moments every day.

379
01:11:02.466 --> 01:11:07.466
You can compare it to being a child, being a father, being a mother, a spouse, or whatever.

380
01:11:07.466 --> 01:11:09.466
You are not continuously together.

381
01:11:09.466 --> 01:11:10.466
You must also work.

382
01:11:10.466 --> 01:11:13.466
You have other matters to occupy yourself with.

383
01:11:13.466 --> 01:11:15.466
And then it is so.

384
01:11:15.466 --> 01:11:20.466
You are not less of a child or father or mother or spouse.

385
01:11:20.466 --> 01:11:23.466
You are not less because of that.

386
01:11:23.466 --> 01:11:25.466
You remain, that is. You are it.

387
01:11:25.466 --> 01:11:28.466
And this is also what Jesus gives us.

388
01:11:28.466 --> 01:11:30.466
We may be it.

389
01:11:30.466 --> 01:11:35.466
And we may seize the moments and the quality moments with God.

390
01:11:35.466 --> 01:11:39.466
For it is indeed the intention that we come to Him with hunger and thirst.

391
01:11:39.466 --> 01:11:41.466
And that we fill ourselves.

392
01:11:41.466 --> 01:11:43.466
And then that is for that day.

393
01:11:43.466 --> 01:11:46.466
And day by day is also a gift from God.

394
01:11:46.466 --> 01:11:49.466
And also the daily food, daily drink.

395
01:11:49.466 --> 01:11:52.466
We had manna in the desert before.

396
01:11:52.466 --> 01:11:54.466
Jesus is the bread of life.

397
01:11:54.466 --> 01:11:57.466
And He is the one who gives that to us.

398
01:11:57.466 --> 01:11:59.466
And He also gives us the living water.

399
01:11:59.466 --> 01:12:01.466
And if we open ourselves to Him.

400
01:12:01.466 --> 01:12:03.466
Circumcised of heart.

401
01:12:03.466 --> 01:12:04.466
And we go to him.

402
01:12:04.466 --> 01:12:06.466
And we take those quality time moments with him.

403
01:12:06.466 --> 01:12:08.466
Then he will transform us.

404
01:12:08.466 --> 01:12:10.466
Every day again.

405
01:12:10.466 --> 01:12:12.466
He washes again with the living water.

406
01:12:12.466 --> 01:12:14.466
He washes again with his Word.

407
01:12:14.466 --> 01:12:16.466
He washes again.

408
01:12:16.466 --> 01:12:18.466
It is not brainwashing.

409
01:12:18.466 --> 01:12:20.466
For then it is not the washing of the heart.

410
01:12:20.466 --> 01:12:24.466
We will receive the heart of Jesus if we remain in him.

411
01:12:26.466 --> 01:12:28.466
It will work layer by layer.

412
01:12:28.466 --> 01:12:30.466
With his inexhaustible personality.

413
01:12:30.466 --> 01:12:32.466
And then we will become like him.

414
01:12:34.466 --> 01:12:38.466
This is actually the whole new covenant.

415
01:12:38.466 --> 01:12:41.466
Summarized in a vine.

416
01:12:41.466 --> 01:12:43.466
This is something so beautiful.

417
01:12:43.466 --> 01:12:45.466
He guarantees for us.

418
01:12:45.466 --> 01:12:47.466
For if we graft ourselves into him.

419
01:12:47.466 --> 01:12:49.466
Then he also holds us tight.

420
01:12:49.466 --> 01:12:51.466
And he keeps us.

421
01:12:51.466 --> 01:12:53.466
This teaches us the Bible as well.

422
01:12:53.466 --> 01:12:55.466
He loves us so much.

423
01:12:55.466 --> 01:12:57.466
He wants to keep us up to date.

424
01:12:57.466 --> 01:12:59.466
If we don't do it. Then we don't do it.

425
01:12:59.466 --> 01:13:01.466
Then we don't drink.

426
01:13:01.466 --> 01:13:03.466
But if we do it.

427
01:13:03.466 --> 01:13:05.466
Then he will prune.

428
01:13:05.466 --> 01:13:07.466
That is nice.

429
01:13:07.466 --> 01:13:09.466
That is not nice at all.

430
01:13:09.466 --> 01:13:11.466
But if you know what that plan does.

431
01:13:11.466 --> 01:13:13.466
If it is not pruned.

432
01:13:13.466 --> 01:13:15.466
Then it grows in every direction.

433
01:13:15.466 --> 01:13:17.466
Except the good one.

434
01:13:17.466 --> 01:13:19.466
Then you get such mini raisins.

435
01:13:19.466 --> 01:13:21.466
That are of no use to you.

436
01:13:21.466 --> 01:13:23.466
Actually, pruning is.

437
01:13:23.466 --> 01:13:25.466
Has nothing to do with sin.

438
01:13:25.466 --> 01:13:27.466
What is really sin.

439
01:13:27.466 --> 01:13:29.466
If we are not in that vine.

440
01:13:29.466 --> 01:13:31.466
Do you understand what I mean.

441
01:13:31.466 --> 01:13:33.466
He makes a distinction here.

442
01:13:33.466 --> 01:13:35.466
If we are not in that vine.

443
01:13:35.466 --> 01:13:37.466
Then He sets us aside for a moment.

444
01:13:37.466 --> 01:13:39.466
The same as what Paul says.

445
01:13:39.466 --> 01:13:41.466
Then we are perhaps saved through the fire.

446
01:13:41.466 --> 01:13:43.466
Or not.

447
01:13:43.466 --> 01:13:45.466
It depends on how the situation is.

448
01:13:45.466 --> 01:13:47.466
That is up to God.

449
01:13:47.466 --> 01:13:49.466
But if you look at pruning.

450
01:13:49.466 --> 01:13:51.466
Then we are actually doing what God wants.

451
01:13:51.466 --> 01:13:53.466
And then we are in that vine.

452
01:13:53.466 --> 01:13:55.466
And then He begins to prune.

453
01:13:55.466 --> 01:13:57.466
But what is pruning then?

454
01:13:57.466 --> 01:13:59.466
Pruning is something that has two aspects.

455
01:13:59.466 --> 01:14:01.466
I want to give two things on that.

456
01:14:01.466 --> 01:14:03.466
That is a piece of focus.

457
01:14:03.466 --> 01:14:05.466
Because if you go in all directions.

458
01:14:05.466 --> 01:14:07.466
Except the right one.

459
01:14:07.466 --> 01:14:09.466
Then you can be sure that nothing will come of it.

460
01:14:09.466 --> 01:14:11.466
And a season.

461
01:14:11.466 --> 01:14:13.466
It is also about seasons.

462
01:14:13.466 --> 01:14:15.466
Because every season, every year.

463
01:14:15.466 --> 01:14:17.466
That thing also needs to be completely pruned.

464
01:14:17.466 --> 01:14:19.466
To be prepared again.

465
01:14:19.466 --> 01:14:21.466
For the next season.

466
01:14:21.466 --> 01:14:23.466
And that focus is very important.

467
01:14:23.466 --> 01:14:25.466
Because that focus.

468
01:14:25.466 --> 01:14:27.466
We can have all sorts of good intentions.

469
01:14:27.466 --> 01:14:29.466
And want all sorts of things.

470
01:14:29.466 --> 01:14:31.466
But the good is often the enemy of the very best.

471
01:14:31.466 --> 01:14:33.466
God wants to do just that.

472
01:14:33.466 --> 01:14:35.466
Of what we.

473
01:14:35.466 --> 01:14:37.466
For which He has destined us.

474
01:14:37.466 --> 01:14:39.466
And that is different for all of us.

475
01:14:39.466 --> 01:14:41.466
And that is so beautiful.

476
01:14:41.466 --> 01:14:43.466
Because otherwise it would be a boring mess.

477
01:14:43.466 --> 01:14:45.466
And it is very beautiful to see.

478
01:14:45.466 --> 01:14:47.466
That God wants to give us the focus.

479
01:14:47.466 --> 01:14:49.466
And He does that with care and love.

480
01:14:49.466 --> 01:14:51.466
For every branch.

481
01:14:51.466 --> 01:14:53.466
He trims that.

482
01:14:53.466 --> 01:14:55.466
That hurts.

483
01:14:55.466 --> 01:14:57.466
But it is necessary.

484
01:14:57.466 --> 01:14:59.466
It is absolutely necessary.

485
01:14:59.466 --> 01:15:01.466
And sometimes you also have seasons.

486
01:15:01.466 --> 01:15:03.466
That God says yes.

487
01:15:03.466 --> 01:15:05.466
This part is now finished.

488
01:15:05.466 --> 01:15:07.466
Those fruits.

489
01:15:07.466 --> 01:15:09.466
I take those with me.

490
01:15:09.466 --> 01:15:11.466
And I prepare you for the next season.

491
01:15:11.466 --> 01:15:13.466
And then he makes a very deep cut again.

492
01:15:13.466 --> 01:15:15.466
That hurts extra.

493
01:15:15.466 --> 01:15:17.466
And it can be good.

494
01:15:17.466 --> 01:15:19.466
That sometimes it is necessary.

495
01:15:19.466 --> 01:15:21.466
That your gifts or ministries.

496
01:15:21.466 --> 01:15:23.466
That you once had.

497
